{
  "formatVersion": 2,
  "title": "Venetian blind: travel and slat angle",
  "description": "A long press moves the blind; the motor first turns the slats (closed when going down, open when going up), then moves the blind. A short press at rest turns the slats by one step, and a short press during a movement stops it. The numeric fields send a position and a slat angle (DPT 5.001: 0 % open, 100 % closed). The actuator estimates both from its configured times and reports them after each stop.",
